\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The contrast is the charm. A tiny Netherland Dwarf named after a mythological trickster god creates delightful narrative tension. These names give your rabbit a story and a personality that generic pet names cannot match.\\\"}]]}]\\n44:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"7\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Should rabbit names match their breed's country of origin?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"It is a lovely touch when it works. A Holland Lop with a Dutch name, a French Lop with a French name, or an English Spot with a classic English name creates cultural coherence. However, personality should always trump geography when the two conflict.\\\"}]]}]\\n45:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"8\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What should I avoid when naming a male rabbit?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Avoid names that are hard to distinguish from common rabbit-care words or commands. Also avoid names that sound too similar to other pets in the household. Rabbits are sensitive to sound and can become confused if names overlap with words they hear frequently.\\\"}]]}]\\n46:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"9\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can two male rabbits share a themed pair of names?\\\"}