,null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"The Ultimate Guide to Fluffy Tenrec Names: 70+ Ideas for Every Tenrec Owner\"}],\"$L47\"]}],\"$L48\",\"$L49\"]}]]}]\n41:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4\",\"aria-label\":\"Post navigation\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/horse-names-inspired-by-nature/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group text-left\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500\",\"children\":\"← Previous Post\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary mt-1 line-clamp-1\",\"children\":\"Horse Names Inspired By Nature: 80+ Beautiful Earth-Inspired Ideas\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/best-dog-names-by-breed/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group text-right\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500\",\"children\":\"Next Post →\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary mt-1 line-clamp-1\",\"children\":\"Best Dog Names by Breed: From Chihuahua to Great Dane 🐕\"}]]}]]}]\n42:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 p-6 bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl border border-primary/10 text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\",\"children\":\"🐾 Ready to find the perfect animal name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-600 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Browse our complete collection of 200+ animal name generators — all 100% free.\"}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/animals/\",\"className\":\"inline-block bg-primary text-white font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-primary-dark transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Browse All Animals →\"}]]}]\n43:[\"$\",\"details\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do mythological names work for such a small, domestic pet?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The contrast is the charm. A tiny Netherland Dwarf named after a mythological trickster god creates delightful narrative tension. These names give your rabbit a story and a personality that generic pet names cannot match.\"}]]}]\n44:[\"$\",\"details\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should rabbit names match their breed's country of origin?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"It is a lovely touch when it works. A Holland Lop with a Dutch name, a French Lop with a French name, or an English Spot with a classic English name creates cultural coherence. However, personality should always trump geography when the two conflict.\"}]]}]\n45:[\"$\",\"details\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What should I avoid when naming a male rabbit?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Avoid names that are hard to distinguish from common rabbit-care words or commands. Also avoid names that sound too similar to other pets in the household. Rabbits are sensitive to sound and can become confused if names overlap with words they hear frequently.\"}]]}]\n46:[\"$\",\"details\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can two male rabbits share a themed pair of names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Themed pairs for bonded rabbits are genuinely delightful. Literary pairs like Hazel and Fiver, historical pairs like Lewis and Clark, or mythological pairs like Apollo and Hermes all create a cohesive identity for your rabbit duo. Just ensure each name is distinct enough for the rabbits to recognize individually.\"}]]}]\n47:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"From inspired by sports inspirations to classic favorites, discover 70+ fluffy tenrec names that capture your tenrec's unique personality.\"}]\n48:[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"funny-macaque-names-inspired-by-music-60-funny-ideas-for-your-macaque\",{\"href\":\"/blog/funny-macaque-names-inspired-by-music-60-funny-ideas-for-your-macaque/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl mb-3\",\"children\":\"🐾\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Macaque Names\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Funny Macaque Names Inspired by Music: 60+ Funny Ideas for Your Macaque\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Looking for funny macaque names? Discover 60+ funny ideas inspired by music for your beloved macaque companion.\"}]]}]\n49:[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"the-ultimate-guide-to-quirky-panda-names-120-ideas-for-every-panda-owner\",{\"href\":\"/blog/the-ultimate-guide-to-quirky-panda-names-120-ideas-for-every-panda-owner/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl mb-3\",\"children\":\"🐼\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Panda Names\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"The Ultimate Guide to Quirky Panda Names: 120+ Ideas for Every Panda Owner\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"From breed-specific inspirations to classic favorites, discover 120+ quirky panda names that capture your panda's unique personality.\"}]]}]\n1a:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n17:null\n1c:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Looking for unique rabbit names for male pets? From classic gentleman names to quirky food-inspired picks, discover 80+ distinctive names perfect for your boy bunny with meanings and personality matches.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.json\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"unique rabbit names, male rabbit names, boy bunny names, pet rabbit names, cute rabbit names\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"p:domain_verify\",\"content\":\"acc18c9aa2855ead49c874b6cac9cb61\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"6\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/unique-rabbit-names-for-male-pets/\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Looking for unique rabbit names for male pets? From classic gentleman names to quirky food-inspired picks, discover 80+ distinctive names perfect for your boy bunny with meanings and personality matches.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"article\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Looking for unique rabbit names for male pets? From classic gentleman names to quirky food-inspired picks, discover 80+ distinctive names perfect for your boy bunny with meanings and personality matches.\"}]]\n","/blog/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n9:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/3i2zmhpv5m7u2.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\"],\"\"]\n2a:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/3i2zmhpv5m7u2.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n2b:\"$Sreact.suspense\"\n2:T27b3,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\",\"description\":\"Looking for unique rabbit names for male pets? From classic gentleman names to quirky food-inspired picks, discover 80+ distinctive names perfect for your boy bunny with meanings and personality matches.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-06\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/unique-rabbit-names-for-male-pets/\"},\"wordCount\":1409,\"articleBody\":\"📋 Table of Contents  Why Male Rabbits Deserve Unique Names Male rabbits — bucks — have distinct personalities that set them apart from other pets. They are curious, social, and surprisingly expressive creatures who communicate through ear positions, body language, and a fascinating range of vocalizations from purring to grunting. Unique rabbit names for male pets should reflect these special qualities rather than defaulting to generic small pet names. A rabbit named Thumper or Bugs is perfectly fine, but a rabbit named Atticus or Truffle tells a richer story about who your bunny actually is. Rabbits are the third most popular pet in America after dogs and cats, with approximately 2.2 million pet rabbits in US households according to the American Pet Products Association. Despite this popularity, rabbit-specific naming resources remain surprisingly limited. Most small pet name lists lump rabbits together with hamsters, gerbils, and guinea pigs without acknowledging the distinct personality, intelligence, and social nature of rabbits. This guide fills that gap with 80+ names specifically chosen for male rabbits based on personality type, appearance, and the unique bond between rabbits and their owners. Classic Gentleman Names for Male Rabbits There is something deeply charming about giving a dignified, gentlemanly name to a small, fluffy rabbit. The contrast between formal name and adorable animal creates instant warmth and memorability. Atticus, from To Kill a Mockingbird, suits a wise, calm rabbit who observes the world with quiet intelligence. Theodore, with its built-in nickname Teddy, works for especially cuddly bunnies. Sebastian suggests sophistication and refinement perfect for the rabbit who grooms himself with particular fastidiousness. More classic gentleman names: Winston carries British dignity. Oliver is friendly and approachable. Jasper has a vintage charm that feels both distinguished and playful. Felix means happy or fortunate in Latin — fitting for a rescue rabbit who found a loving home. Hugo suggests literary sophistication. Barnaby feels whimsical and old-fashioned in the best way. Each of these names gives your male rabbit a presence that acknowledges his importance in your household rather than treating him as a minor pet. Food-Inspired Boy Bunny Names Rabbits are famously food-motivated creatures, and naming your male rabbit after something delicious is both accurate and adorable. Food names for rabbits have the added benefit of naturally suiting their round, soft bodies and their genuine enthusiasm for mealtime. Truffle suggests something rare, precious, and utterly delightful — much like your rabbit. Mochi captures that soft, squishy, sweet quality that makes rabbits so huggable. Biscuit is warm, comforting, and universally beloved. Beyond the obvious choices, consider cuisine-specific food names that tell a story. Pesto suggests herbal freshness and Italian warmth. Kimchi adds Korean spice and personality. Wasabi packs surprising heat into a small package — perfect for a tiny rabbit with a big attitude. Chai brings aromatic complexity. Tofu describes a white rabbit's coloring while being genuinely cute. Nori suits darker-colored rabbits. Each of these names rewards cultural knowledge while remaining accessible and memorable. Nature & Woodland Names for Male Rabbits Rabbits are creatures of meadows, forests, and fields, making nature-inspired names a natural and beautiful fit. Woodland names connect your domestic rabbit to their wild cousins — the cottontails, hares, and European rabbits that inspired countless folktales and children's stories. Thistle evokes quiet meadows and gentle breezes. Clover connects to the rabbit's favorite treat and symbolizes good fortune. Bracken suggests the dappled forest floor where wild rabbits make their homes. Forest-inspired names: Cedar, Oak, Birch, and Rowan all carry the strength and steadfastness of trees while remaining gentle enough for a small animal. Meadow and Glen paint pastoral landscapes in a single word. River suggests movement, life, and natural beauty. These names bring a touch of the wild into your home while honoring your rabbit's evolutionary heritage and natural instincts. How to Pick the Perfect Male Rabbit Name Observing your rabbit for a few days before deciding on a name is genuinely worth the patience. Male rabbits reveal their personalities through consistent patterns: some are bold explorers who investigate every corner, others are cautious observers who prefer to watch from a safe distance. Some demand attention through gentle nose nudges, while others express affection through quiet proximity. The right name will naturally emerge from watching who your rabbit actually is rather than who you expected them to be. Practical considerations matter too. Short names with clear consonant sounds are easier for rabbits to recognize — they may not come when called like dogs, but rabbits absolutely learn to associate specific sounds with food, attention, and positive experiences. Test your top choices by saying them during treat time for a few days each. The name that feels most natural when you say it, paired with a happy rabbit who associates it with good things, is almost certainly the winner. Literary & Historical Male Rabbit Names Literature and history offer a rich vein of distinguished names for male rabbits. Peter, from Beatrix Potter's beloved tales, is so iconic that it has become nearly synonymous with rabbits themselves. But beyond Peter, Potter's world provides Benjamin, the loyal cousin, and Mr. McGregor's garden-raiding crew of Flopsy, Mopsy, and Cottontail — though those skew feminine, their charm is undeniable for any rabbit. From broader literature: Hazel and Fiver from Watership Down are perhaps the most dignified rabbit names in all of fiction. Hazel, the thoughtful leader, and Fiver, the anxious prophet, give your rabbit literary gravitas. From history: Napoleon suits a particularly ambitious, determined rabbit who conquers every obstacle course and treat puzzle you set before him. Aristotle works for the contemplative rabbit who seems to study the world with philosophical depth. These names elevate your rabbit from pet to personality with genuine cultural weight. Mythology-Inspired Male Rabbit Names Rabbits appear frequently in world mythology, often as clever tricksters, moon-dwelling companions, or symbols of fertility and renewal. The Moon Rabbit appears across Chinese, Japanese, and Korean folklore — a rabbit who lives on the moon, pounding the elixir of life. Names drawn from lunar mythology — Tsuki (Japanese for moon), Selene (Greek moon goddess, adaptable for males), or simply Moon — connect your rabbit to these ancient and beautiful stories. Trickster rabbits appear in African and Native American folklore. Br'er Rabbit from African American folktales is clever, resourceful, and always one step ahead of larger predators. Nanabozho from Ojibwe tradition is a shapeshifting rabbit spirit. Kokopelli, while typically depicted as a flute-playing figure, is associated with fertility and renewal — fitting for the famously reproductive rabbit. These mythological names give your rabbit a connection to centuries of storytelling tradition. Caring for Your Named Rabbit: Tips for New Owners Once you have chosen the perfect unique name for your male rabbit, the real work of rabbit care begins. Rabbits are social, intelligent animals who thrive on routine, enrichment, and gentle handling. Spend at least two hours of supervised out-of-cage time with your rabbit daily. Use their name consistently during feeding, play, and cuddle sessions — rabbits absolutely learn to associate their names with positive experiences, and consistent usage strengthens that bond enormously over time. Male rabbits, especially once neutered, are often more affectionate and people-oriented than females. They tend to be more relaxed about handling and more eager for human interaction. This makes the naming process even more rewarding — your rabbit will genuinely learn to recognize and respond to the name you choose. For the best results, pair the name with a specific tone of voice and a small healthy treat like a tiny piece of banana or apple. Within weeks, your uniquely named boy bunny will come hopping when called, cementing the bond between name and animal in the most satisfying possible way. Explore our name generators for {anatolian-leopard}, {antechinus}, {american-black-bear}, {aldabra-giant-tortoise}, and {alligator-gar} to find the perfect name for your companion. Whether you are naming a new pet today or just exploring ideas for the future, the most important principle remains the same: the best name is the one that feels right to you and fits your specific animal. Take your time, involve your family in the process, and trust that the perfect name will reveal itself through patience and attention. Every great pet deserves a great name — and every great name starts with a thoughtful owner who cares enough to get it right. For thousands more name ideas across hundreds of animal species, browse our complete collection at bestanimalnames.com, where every name is hand-picked and every generator is 100 percent free.\",\"image\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-unique-rabbit-names-for-male-pets.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2\"}}],\"$L3\",\"$L4\",\"$L5\",\"$L6\"],null,\"$L7\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"Vn-m7ZnH220y8-FGOgPuM\"}\n8:Tff3,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do rabbits actually recognize their names?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, rabbits can learn to recognize their names, especially when associated with positive reinforcement like treats and gentle petting. While they do not come when called as reliably as dogs, many rabbits clearly respond to their names through ear movement, head turning, or approaching their owners when called.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Should I name my rabbit based on its color or personality?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Both approaches work well. Color-based names like Snowball or Cocoa are intuitive and descriptive. Personality-based names like Rascal or Snuggles feel more personal and unique. Many owners combine both approaches — observing their rabbit's coloring and personality for a few days before deciding.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How long should a rabbit's name be?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"One to two syllables is ideal for recognition and daily use. Names like Thumper, Clover, Mochi, and Theo are easy to say and for rabbits to distinguish. Longer names will naturally be shortened in daily use — maximize the odds that the shortened version is still a name you love.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can two male rabbits live together with different names?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Male rabbits can live together successfully when both are neutered and properly bonded. Choose names with distinctly different sounds to help your rabbits identify which name applies to whom. Avoid rhyming pairs that create confusion during feeding and interaction.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the most popular male rabbit names?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Thumper remains the most popular by far, followed by Bugs, Peter (from Peter Rabbit), Oreo, and Snowball. Unique names like Truffle, Atticus, Mochi, and Clover are rapidly growing in popularity as rabbit owners seek more distinctive options.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I use a female literary character name for my male rabbit?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Absolutely. Literary names transcend gender, and rabbits certainly do not care about the gender of their namesakes. A male rabbit named Hazel (from Watership Down, where Hazel is male) or even literary names typically coded female can work beautifully if they suit your rabbit's personality.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do mythological names work for such a small, domestic pet?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The contrast is the charm. A tiny Netherland Dwarf named after a mythological trickster god creates delightful narrative tension. These names give your rabbit a story and a personality that generic pet names cannot match.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Should rabbit names match their breed's country of origin?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"It is a lovely touch when it works. A Holland Lop with a Dutch name, a French Lop with a French name, or an English Spot with a classic English name creates cultural coherence. However, personality should always trump geography when the two conflict.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What should I avoid when naming a male rabbit?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Avoid names that are hard to distinguish from common rabbit-care words or commands. Also avoid names that sound too similar to other pets in the household. Rabbits are sensitive to sound and can become confused if names overlap with words they hear frequently.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can two male rabbits share a themed pair of names?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Themed pairs for bonded rabbits are genuinely delightful. Literary pairs like Hazel and Fiver, historical pairs like Lewis and Clark, or mythological pairs like Apollo and Hermes all create a cohesive identity for your rabbit duo. Just ensure each name is distinct enough for the rabbits to recognize individually.\"}}]}3:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$8\"}}]\n4:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Blog\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/unique-rabbit-names-for-male-pets/\\\"}]}\"}}]\n5:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-500 flex gap-1 flex-wrap\",\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Blog\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 font-medium\",\"children\":\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\"}]]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-6xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"🐰\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Rabbit Names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"2026-06-06\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-500\",\"children\":\"By BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Unique Rabbit Names For Male Pets: 80+ Handpicked Ideas\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"Looking for unique rabbit names for male pets? From classic gentleman names to quirky food-inspired picks, discover 80+ distinctive names perfect for your boy bunny with meanings and personality matches.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 mt-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"unique rabbit names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"unique rabbit names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"male rabbit names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"male rabbit names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"boy bunny names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"boy bunny names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"pet rabbit names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"pet rabbit names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"cute rabbit names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"cute rabbit names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"📋 Table of Contents\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/5 to-indigo-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/10 mb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\",\"children\":\"📋 Table of Contents\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 list-none pl-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[1,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\